{"authored" [{"question" "q-161134" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,v,\\,v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ Use the scalar surface-area factor $\\|r_u\\times r_v\\|$ with its absolute values for the stated parameter domain. What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{8}|u|.$*" "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161134/review.json" "file_sha256" "57ccb5732b22d7fe0f2579d6ebe308fc29242740acb1a8e84503226dcc79087a" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161134/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "174cea456a2a0aa61f80f7d1aad565037218c7f6c12b3e224c45291fd1a440ea" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161134/verification.json" "basis" 2165 "rationale" "The Euclidean norm requires an absolute value of the parameter. Keep the original general domain, correct its area factor and derivation, and add the absolute-value answer with a new field version, retaining the old field, choices, key and history. q161286 uses sqrt8|v|; q161134 uses sqrt8|u|."} {"question" "q-161134" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The scalar surface-area factor is nonnegative. For $r(u,v)=(u^2,v,v)$,\n\n$$r_u=(2u,0,0),\\qquad r_v=(0,1,1),\\qquad r_u\\times r_v=(0,-2u,2u).$$\n\nHence\n\n$$\\|r_u\\times r_v\\|=\\sqrt{8u^2}=\\sqrt8\\,|u|.$$\n\nSubstitution into $f(x,y,z)=x^2y^2z^2$ gives\n\n$$f(r(u,v))=(u^2)^2v^2v^2=u^4v^4.$$\n\nThe missing integrand for the stated general parameter domain is therefore\n\n$$\\sqrt8\\,u^4v^4|u|.$$\n\nThe original hint and source key used $\\sqrt8\\,u$ and $\\sqrt8\\,u^5v^4$, respectively, without restricting $u$. They are valid for $u\\ge0$ but fail for negative $u$. At $(u,v)=(-1,1)$ the correct integrand is $\\sqrt8$; the signed source expression gives $-\\sqrt8$, although the scalar function is nonnegative. This correction retains the original general domain, fixes the hint, and adds the absolute-value choice.\n\nThe parametrization loses rank at $u=0$. The displayed surface-integral equality has the usual requirement of regular patches and no multiple coverage except on negligible boundaries; the local area factor remains $\\sqrt8|u|$." "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161134/review.json" "file_sha256" "57ccb5732b22d7fe0f2579d6ebe308fc29242740acb1a8e84503226dcc79087a" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161134/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "174cea456a2a0aa61f80f7d1aad565037218c7f6c12b3e224c45291fd1a440ea" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161134/verification.json" "basis" 2165 "rationale" "The Euclidean norm requires an absolute value of the parameter. Keep the original general domain, correct its area factor and derivation, and add the absolute-value answer with a new field version, retaining the old field, choices, key and history. q161286 uses sqrt8|v|; q161134 uses sqrt8|u|."} {"question" "q-161134" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{4}{v}^{4}|u|"] "category" "mathematical_correction" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161134/review.json" "file_sha256" "57ccb5732b22d7fe0f2579d6ebe308fc29242740acb1a8e84503226dcc79087a" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161134/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "174cea456a2a0aa61f80f7d1aad565037218c7f6c12b3e224c45291fd1a440ea" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/mathematical-corrections/q-161134/verification.json" "basis" 2165 "rationale" "The Euclidean norm requires an absolute value of the parameter. Keep the original general domain, correct its area factor and derivation, and add the absolute-value answer with a new field version, retaining the old field, choices, key and history. q161286 uses sqrt8|v|; q161134 uses sqrt8|u|."} {"question" "q-161134" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,v,\\,v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{8}u.$*" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065891/state.json" "file_sha256" "bdfa6a803b0f5b4dd40bc4cb5a6a37fd1c18de08705f0016275ee683974ae5bf" "basis" 2162 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065891/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161134" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{8}u.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =({x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2})\\,{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =({u}^{2}\\cdot {u}^{2})\\cdot {v}^{2}\\cdot {v}^{2}\\, \\\\  & ={u}^{4}{v}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{5}{v}^{4}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065891/state.json" "file_sha256" "bdfa6a803b0f5b4dd40bc4cb5a6a37fd1c18de08705f0016275ee683974ae5bf" "basis" 2162 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065891/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-161134" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065891/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b20e1f45a42d5fede32fa998c7066f7dd3766d8c34d0223df22b1ac471cd7d6e" "basis" 2162 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14065891/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [] "usage" {"q-161134" []} "basis" 2165 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186351031 17592186351032 17592186351033 17592186351034 17592186351035 17592186351171] "immutable_fields" [[17592186351170 :answer-field/correct] [17592186351170 :answer-field/id] [17592186351170 :answer-field/key] [17592186351170 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
